Author:     Dennis Dyall Wallin <dennis@dyallo.se>
AuthorDate: Wed Nov 4 21:08:29 2026 +0100
Commit:     Dennis Dyall Wallin <dennis@dyallo.se>
CommitDate: Wed Nov 4 21:08:29 2026 +0100

    fix(core,piv)!: clear response data through explicit buffer ownership
    
    Make ApduResponse a sealed owner with copied input and idempotent Clear, so aliases are cleared without writable casts or modifying caller buffers. Keep PIV crypto/data-object buffers mutable until transfer and expose owned result Memory to recipients. Replace PIV read-only-to-writable cleanup with owner-mediated clearing.
    
    Verify both response constructors, preserved aliases, caller isolation, crypto ownership transfer, and existing PIV cleanup tests. Core units: 1718 passed/4 existing skips; PIV units: 264 passed. A finalizer probe timed out once in the full unit run and passed both focused and full Core reruns without source changes.

