index 0e0e301e..b822163a 100644
--- a/src/Piv/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/src/Piv/CLAUDE.md
@@ -67,6 +67,11 @@ success responses therefore resolve as `Failed`, and raw or untransferred parsed
 
 ## Critical Security Requirements
 
+Raw APDU responses have a Core-owned `Clear()` operation. Internal crypto/data-object results stay in owned
+`byte[]` buffers until the public session transfers `Memory<byte>` to the caller. Never cast read-only memory
+writable to perform cleanup. Clear only buffers owned by this scope; caller inputs and static defaults remain
+borrowed and unmodified.
+
 PIV handles PINs, PUKs, management keys, private keys, and cryptographic operation payloads.
 
 - Zero PINs, PUKs, management keys, and encoded sensitive APDU payloads with `CryptographicOperations.ZeroMemory()`.
diff --git a/src/Piv/README.md b/src/Piv/README.md
index 3acfcacd..e57aa48c 100644
--- a/src/Piv/README.md
+++ b/src/Piv/README.md
@@ -170,6 +170,11 @@ development firmware retains Core's permissive compatibility handling.
 
 ## Security notes
 
+- Crypto, raw data-object, and temporary-PIN results transfer writable `Memory<byte>` to the caller.
+  Clear owned plaintext, shared secrets, and temporary PINs with `CryptographicOperations.ZeroMemory(result.Span)`
+  after use. This replaces read-only result memory from earlier previews. Internal parsers retain mutable
+  owned buffers until transfer; raw APDU responses are cleared through their owner's `Clear()` method.
+
 - PINs, PUKs, management keys, and temporary PINs cross the API as `ReadOnlyMemory<byte>`. The session never
   zeroes a buffer you passed in; zero it yourself with `CryptographicOperations.ZeroMemory` in a `finally`.
 - Never log PINs, PUKs, management keys, plaintexts, or signatures. Log metadata only.
